+<section class="band" id="implementation-cost"><div class="wrap"><div class="head reveal"><p class="kicker">3 · Cost analysis</p><h2>Staged costs and affordability</h2></div><div class="reveal"><h3>Basis and scope</h3><p>Capital expenditure (CAPEX) covers equipment and setup; operating expenditure (OPEX) covers services while active. Q190 core equipment is 13,933,146 VND per station, or 43,482,944 VND for three stations and one optional shared pH kit. These hardware subtotals exclude the remaining pilot costs. The budget uses a historical 25,940 VND/USD assumption, not a current transaction rate (<a href="#references">DFRobot, n.d.-a, n.d.-c</a>; <a href="#references">Hshop, n.d.-c</a>; <a href="#references">LILYGO, n.d.</a>; <a href="#references">NDH, n.d.</a>).</p><p>The 36-month project starts one station before two more at illustrative month six. The 100W/40Ah power configuration and unquoted items are planning assumptions. Listed prices, market benchmarks and internal allowances are distinguished in Appendix E; simulated results do not establish field performance.</p><div class="costsum"><div><small>Station 1</small><b data-cost="first">₫13,933,146</b><p>Core equipment</p></div><div><small>Next two stations</small><b data-cost="rest">₫27,866,292</b><p>Core equipment</p></div><div><small>One shared pH kit</small><b data-cost="spare">₫1,683,506</b><p>Included planning reserve</p></div><div><small>Three stations + kit</small><b data-cost="total">₫43,482,944</b><p>Partial hardware subtotal</p></div></div></div><div class="reveal"><h3>Three-year budget</h3><p>Table 4 estimates 339,314,885 VND including 20% contingency. Its low–high scenarios reflect different allowances, not guaranteed prices. Labour uses 600,000 VND per person-day, informed by published electrical-work benchmarks. Future prices are held constant for comparison (<a href="#references">FDI Care, n.d.</a>; <a href="#references">Viễn Thông Tia Sáng, n.d.</a>).</p><p>Thirty-six monthly field rounds include pH calibration, DO cleaning and the six testing rounds; 16 station checks are not extra journeys. Early DO/turbidity calibration every two months stays within 90 days. Shared hosting is counted once. Renewal, incidents, delivery, supply-tax uncertainty and disposal have separate allowances; full-probe DO reserves cover unavailable cap pricing (<a href="#references">DFRobot, n.d.-c, n.d.-d, 2026</a>; <a href="#references">Render, n.d.-b</a>).</p><div id="planning-summary" role="region" tabindex="0" aria-label="Table 4. Modelled pilot budget (VND); estimates, not supplier quotations; scroll horizontally" style="overflow-x:auto;max-width:100%"><table style="width:100%;min-width:580px"><caption>Table 4. Modelled pilot budget (VND); estimates, not supplier quotations</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Category</th><th scope="col">Three-year VND</th><th scope="col">Scope</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CAPEX</td><td>91,660,428</td><td>Equipment, setup and supply reserve</td></tr><tr><td>OPEX</td><td>143,606,000</td><td>Staff, field routes, services and consumables</td></tr><tr><td>Lifecycle</td><td>47,495,976</td><td>Parts reserves and collection</td></tr><tr><td>Subtotal</td><td>282,762,404</td><td>Before general contingency</td></tr><tr><td>Contingency (20%)</td><td>56,552,481</td><td>Analyst reserve</td></tr><tr><td>Three-year planning budget</td><td>339,314,885</td><td>Estimate; not a quotation</td></tr><tr><td>Low–high scenario</td><td>260,250,806–468,154,608</td><td>Alternative assumptions; not a price ceiling</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="note"><b>Three-year planning budget: <span data-budget="totalVnd">₫339,314,885</span></b></p></div><div class="reveal"><h3>Affordability and payment proposal</h3><p>A proposed municipal or institutional pilot fund would cover setup. Operations and renewal average about 5.31 million VND per project-month before contingency. This proposal charges households no monitoring fee and assumes no grant, income or unpaid labour. These are proposed funding roles, not commitments; income evidence does not establish affordability. If recurring funding is insufficient, retain one pilot and defer expansion.</p><p>Ordering the next two stations requires acceptance and an updated budget. Field power, coverage and repair capacity remain untested; the 48-hour response target is not a contracted service. Contingency does not guarantee performance or unlimited incident coverage.</p></div><div class="reveal"><h3>Supporting records</h3><p><a href="#appendices-cost">Appendix E: budget, sources and assumptions</a> · <a href="/documents/ba-nguyen-cost-submission-2026-11-28.docx" download>Cost section and appendices (Word)</a></p></div></div></section>

